			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Add URI resolution, extension reinstall, text document open, window title, and diagnostic marker handlers\n\nImplement missing IPC command handlers and a gRPC notification bridge to improve VS Code extension compatibility and editor integration.\n\nIPC additions in WindServiceHandlers:\n- `env:asExternalUri` / `env:resolveExternalUri` - pass-through URI resolution so extension-provided URIs work without a registered opener\n- `extensions:reinstall` - returns minimal ILocalExtension envelope preventing ExtensionManagementService retries (no gallery backend)\n- `text:open` / `workspace:openTextDocument` - relays open intent to Sky via Tauri event so Monaco loads the document and emits onDidOpenTextDocument\n- `window:setTitle` / `nativeHost:setTitle` - explicit title override from extensions or workbench title service\n- `nativeHost:setDocumentEdited` - visual dirty-dot proxy by prefixing window title with '•' since Tauri 2.x lacks NSWindow::setDocumentEdited\n- `language:getLanguages` / `languages:getLanguages` - returns hardcoded language identifier list for extension API compatibility\n\ngRPC addition in MountainVinegRPCService:\n- `markers.change` / `language.markers.change` - receives diagnostic marker updates from Cocoon and forwards to Mountain's DiagnosticManager via Environment.SetDiagnostics\n\nImpact: Closes gaps in extension host IPC surface, enables document opening from Cocoon, provides window title control, and wires diagnostic marker streaming from the extension host to the native backend.",
			"SHA": "910b3cc89d4d2b685d05aaca35e150c51efdf03a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-10T12:45:39Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1768,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement bidirectional streaming channel for Cocoon gRPC service\n\nThe `open_channel_from_mountain` RPC was a stub returning `Unimplemented` since the multiplexer wiring was deferred to a later patch. This change provides the full bidirectional streaming implementation so Cocoon can open a persistent stream and exchange Envelope frames with Mountain without falling back to unary endpoints.\n\nKey modifications:\n- Add `NEXT_CHANNEL_ID` atomic counter and `CHANNEL_REGISTRY` (DashMap) to track per-stream outbound senders\n- Implement stream handler that reads inbound frames and routes: Notification → GenericNotification::Dispatcher, Request → GenericRequest::Dispatcher with response sent back via the registered mpsc channel, Response → dropped (unexpected direction), Cancel → no-op\n- Spawn read pump as detached Tauri async task so the method returns the outbound stream immediately\n- Clean up registry entry on stream termination\n\nImpact: Enables low-latency bidirectional communication between Mountain and the Cocoon extension host, removing the need for polling or repeated unary calls for streaming workloads.",
			"SHA": "4853ac85e2cc627cbd26e696a77b5d1ab9b93d61"
		},
